{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stable-jobless-coot","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Symptom\n\nThe scheduled `Verify Authorship Identity` workflow has failed on consecutive scheduled runs:\n\n- run 35192575898 at 2026-09-17T07:02:22Z\n- run 35224107600 at 2026-09-17T12:57:24Z (head `5b143d9b15ba45509757f125126132c34c9dfe53`)\n\nThe failing job is `verify-identity (authenticated-authorship gate)`; the failing step is \"Fail closed if the blobless checkout pack exceeds its limit\". The error is exact:\n\n```\ncheckout pack is 648505 KiB; limit is 563200 KiB\n```\n\nwith `REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 563200` in the step environment. The overage is roughly 85 MiB, about 15% over the limit.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThis is the authenticated-authorship gate. It fails **closed** by design, so while it is red the gate is not verifying authorship at all — it is aborting before it gets there. A gate that always fails provides no signal, and a standing red scheduled run trains readers to ignore it. Both scheduled runs on 2026-09-17 failed, so this is a persistent condition rather than a flake.\n\n## Investigation required before any fix\n\nThe limit is deliberately a fail-closed bound, so raising the number is a fix only if the growth is legitimate. The investigation must distinguish:\n\n1. **Legitimate growth** — the repository's blobless pack has grown organically past a bound that was set when the repo was smaller, and the bound needs to track repo size.\n2. **Debris** — a large blob, an accidentally committed artifact, or a packing regression inflated the pack. In that case raising the limit hides the real defect.\n\nEstablish which by measuring the pack's composition (largest objects and their paths) and by finding when the pack crossed the limit relative to the bound's last change. Do not change the limit before that question is answered.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The root cause is identified as either legitimate growth or specific debris, with the measurement that distinguishes them recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] If debris: the offending objects are named and removed or excluded, and the pack measures under the limit.\n- [ ] If legitimate growth: the bound is adjusted with a recorded rationale tying it to observed repository size, including headroom for expected growth.\n- [ ] A regression guard exists so the next approach to the limit is visible before the gate turns red.\n- [ ] `Verify Authorship Identity` passes on a scheduled run after the change lands.\n","id":"f5ac-391c-ec70-4fa9","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Verify Authorship Identity fails closed: blobless checkout pack exceeded its limit"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789668213464836418,"uuid":"f84ae7b2-d61b-45ba-975c-1cc1cb6b248a"}